SUMMARY:Private Lunch w/ Matt Botvinick [Anthropic; AI & Rule of Law]
DESCRIPTION:A private lunch with SAILS and Matt Botvinick\, who leads the AI & Rule of Law Team at the Anthropic Institute. This team\, embedded within Anthropic\, conducts research on what AI will mean for executive power\, for courts and elections\, and for the public deliberation that constitutional democracy ultimately rests on. Matt is also a Resident Fellow at Yale Law School and previously was a Senior Director of Research at Google DeepMind and Professor in Neural Computation at Princeton.\n\nNote: attendance to this lunch is limited to 15 students from the Stanford Law School community. Space is limited\, so please only register if you are deeply interested in participating in a discussion at the intersection of artificial intelligence and the rule of law. Attendees will be chosen via a lottery system.\n\nEnter Lottery To Attend — Thursday\, October 8\, 2026\, 12:00 to 1:00pm.\n\nhttps://law.stanford.edu/event/private-lunch-w-matt-botvinick-anthropic-ai-rule-of-law/\n\nThis is a Stanford Law School community event.\n\nEnter Lottery To Attend: https://forms.gle/GDY8Q69BbM3geEom7
URL:https://law.stanford.edu/event/private-lunch-w-matt-botvinick-anthropic-ai-rule-of-law/
LOCATION:@ SLS: Room 272\, Crown Quadrangle\, 559 Nathan Abbott Way\, Stanford\, CA\, 94305-8610\, United States
CATEGORIES:Lunchtime Speakers
GEO:37.424106;-122.1660756
